Chapter 17
Payback, the profitability index and capital rationing
فترة الاسترداد ومؤشر الربحية وترشيد رأس المال
Net present value answers the question "does this create value?" and the internal rate of return answers "at what rate?". Two other questions get asked in every real investment meeting, and neither of the Chapter 16 measures answers them: how long before we get our money back, and what do we do when there is not enough money for everything?
This chapter answers both. Payback and discounted payback measure the speed of recovery; the profitability index measures value for each dollar committed and is the tool for rationing; and the accounting rate of return, which discounts nothing, closes the chapter because the exam still asks for it and because the budget committee often starts with it.
Figure F717-01 is your map.
Figure F717-01. Chapter 17 roadmap: speed of recovery, value per dollar, and what to do when money is short.
