LANGUAGE FOCUS   "Payback" and "index"
English payback is a compound of ordinary words and sounds like plain speech, which is why it survives in boardrooms that have never discounted anything. The danger is that it sounds like a verdict — "the project pays back" — when it is only a duration. Arabic فترة الاسترداد keeps the word فترة, period, in the term itself, so the Arabic cannot be mistaken for a judgment; French délai de récupération does the same with délai. Index in profitability index means a ratio to a base, as in the index numbers of statistics, and the base here is the money invested. Note that Arabic مؤشر and French indice both mean an indicator rather than a measure of profit, which is the right instinct: the index indicates where to put scarce money and does not measure how much profit there is.
